            "long": "Another chance to hear BjÃ¶rk share her musical milestones with Matt Everitt.\n\nPublicly and critically acclaimed, BjÃ¶rk has 13 Grammy Awards nominations, one Academy Award and two Golden Globe Awards to her name, but it's her ability to use her distinct singing voice as an instrument to craft unique melodies that has won her millions of fans over the world.\n\nBjÃ¶rk talks Matt Everitt through her remarkable career. She discusses first falling in love with music after being fascinated by the artwork of her parents' collection of Joni Mitchell and Frank Zappa LPs, recording her debut album aged just 11, forming the Sugarcubes, working with Thom Yorke and what inspires her to return to the studio and the stage.\n\nFirst broadcast in September 2011."
